meta {
  name: List Notifications
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?page=1&size=20
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  size: 20
  ~unreadOnly: false
  ~search:
}

docs {
  The dropdown contents, newest first. Call this when the bell is clicked rather
  than rendering from whatever the socket happened to deliver — a page refresh
  would otherwise empty the list.
  
  `page` (default 1), `size` (default 20, clamped to a maximum of 100),
  `unreadOnly` (default false), `search` (case-insensitive contains-match
  against title and body; ANDed with `unreadOnly`).
  
  Success (200): `data` is a PagedResult of notifications, each carrying
  notificationGuid, typeCode, title, body, entityType, entityGuid,
  parentEntityGuid, isRead, createdDate.
  
  The frontend builds its deep link from `entityType` + `entityGuid` — the
  backend deliberately stores no URL, so renaming a route cannot break
  historical notifications. For ENQUIRY_CREATED the target is
  /admissions/enquiry-followup?enquiry={entityGuid}.
}
